%%{init: {"flowchart": {"htmlLabels": true}} }%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Browser / Mobile App
    participant APIGW as API Gateway<br/>(Cognito User Pool Authorizer)
    participant JWKS as Cognito User Pool<br/>JWKS endpoint
    participant Lambda as Backend Lambda<br/>(optional)
    participant DB as App backend

    Note over Client,JWKS: 1. User signs in (Hosted UI or initiate_auth)
    Client->>APIGW: GET /items<br/>Authorization: Bearer <id_token>

    Note over APIGW: 2. Authorizer needs the signing key
    APIGW->>JWKS: GET /.well-known/jwks.json<br/>(cached, ~5 min TTL)
    JWKS-->>APIGW: 200 { "keys": [{ "kid": "abc", "n": "...", "e": "AQAB" }] }

    Note over APIGW: 3. Verify signature with the JWK
    Note over APIGW: 4. Check claims: exp, iss, aud, token_use
    Note over APIGW: 5. Extract sub / cognito:groups / scope

    alt token valid
        APIGW->>Lambda: invoke with x-amzn-oidc-* headers
        Lambda->>DB: business logic
        DB-->>Lambda: data
        Lambda-->>APIGW: 200 + JSON
        APIGW-->>Client: 200 OK + body
    else token missing / invalid / expired
        APIGW-->>Client: 401 Unauthorized<br/>(WWW-Authenticate: Bearer)
    end
